module oh-state-rules

/// `lit/oh-rules` is a base library: it declares what Ohio's court
/// packages share and no procedure of its own. Its pack holds only this
/// placeholder terminal, which no link or case may route through.
start library

terminal library: "Ohio state court rules library (no procedure)"

/// An initial brief of an appellant or cross-appellant, or an answer brief
/// of an appellee or cross-appellee: at most 9,000 words without prior
/// leave, exclusive of the cover page, tables, statement regarding oral
/// argument, certificates, signature blocks and appendices; 30 pages at
/// 12-point font are presumed compliant, and a court of appeals may adopt
/// different limits by local rule (App.R. 19(A)).
limit merit-brief { words <= 9000 cite "App.R. 19(A)" } cite "App.R. 19(A)"
/// A reply brief: at most 4,500 words on the same terms; 15 pages at
/// 12-point font are presumed compliant (App.R. 19(A)).
limit reply-brief { words <= 4500 cite "App.R. 19(A)" } cite "App.R. 19(A)"
/// An application for reconsideration, en banc consideration or both, and
/// any response to it: at most 15 pages unless the court or a local rule
/// allows otherwise (App.R. 26(A)(1)).
limit reconsideration-application { pages <= 15 cite "App.R. 26(A)" } cite "App.R. 26(A)"

// The trigger events the court packages' graphs route on.
/// An action, claim, petition or charge is filed and the proceeding begins.
event ActionCommenced()
/// A final judgment, decision or appealable order is entered.
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A notice of appeal, or a petition or appeal for review of a lower court's or tribunal's decision, is filed.
event NoticeOfAppealFiled()
/// The record on appeal or review is filed or transmitted.
event RecordFiled()
/// The reviewing court's or tribunal's decision or opinion is filed.
event DecisionFiled()
/// A petition for discretionary review in a higher court (certiorari, transfer, leave or review) is filed.
event ReviewPetitionFiled()
/// The mandate, remittitur or certificate of judgment issues.
event MandateIssued()
